Q1. What is Inheritance? Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

Inheritance is an OOP concept in which one class
(Child/Subclass) acquires the accessible properties
(fields) and behaviors (methods) of another class
(Parent/Superclass).

Inheritance represents an "IS-A" relationship.

Java uses the

extends

keyword to achieve inheritance.

Why do we need it?

• Code Reusability.
• Reduce Code Duplication.
• Improve Maintainability.
• Support Method Overriding.
• Enable Runtime Polymorphism.
• Organize code hierarchically.

Real-Life Example

Vehicle
    |
-----------------
|       |       |
Car    Bike    Truck

All inherit common properties like

• Engine
• Tyres
• start()

Software Industry Example

class User{

    String name;
    String email;

    void login(){

    }
}

class Customer extends User{

}

class Admin extends User{

}

Customer and Admin reuse common functionality from User.

