Q4. What is the difference between IS-A and HAS-A
relationship?

Interview Ready Answer

IS-A Relationship

• Represents Inheritance.
• Implemented using extends.
• Child is a specialized version of Parent.

Examples

Dog IS-A Animal

Car IS-A Vehicle

Java Example

class Animal{

}

class Dog extends Animal{

}

------------------------------------------------------------

HAS-A Relationship

• Represents Composition/Aggregation.
• One class contains an object of another class.
• Implemented by creating object as a member.

Examples

Car HAS-A Engine

Computer HAS-A CPU

House HAS-A Room

Java Example

class Engine{

}

class Car{

    private Engine engine=new Engine();

}

